  "scope": "Actual macOS arm64 HTTPS surface/rotation/routing and proxy checks, supplemented by25 current Linux/Lima-to-Mac remote-client wire checks. No Ubuntu server installation, named external host/provider, browser/media or whole-gate acceptance qualification is claimed.",
  "implementation": [
    "Optional CanonicalServerConfig.https exposes at most four unique named surface bindings, disabled by default. Public origins are exact HTTPS contacts; Remote requires explicit network profile/origin. Certificate name checks precede installation recovery/binding. Local HTTP remains loopback.",
    "Application, administration, Telnyx callback and minimal health routes are separate. Existing shared Store/Service authority, original IDs, protected issuance/record response writers and bounded bodies remain installed. Only application allows explicitly configured browser origins; administrative/provider-context requests keep their existing Origin refusals.",
    "Host must match the configured public authority. Forwarding accepts a complete single-hop X-Forwarded-Proto=https/Host/numeric-For tuple only from an exact configured immediate socket-peer IP, then strips it. It cannot authenticate. Known identity assertions, RFC Forwarded and port/prefix rewriting are refused.",
    "TLS listeners bound pending five-second handshakes and live TCP sockets by configured connection capacity. Existing protected physical response custody is retained until actual IO closure. Public HTTPS workers participate in readiness and owned shutdown.",
    "serve installs SIGHUP handling before ready reporting, performs explicit off-executor TLS reload from original configured files, retains last-good identity on invalid replacement, and drains on SIGTERM/SIGINT. Endpoints are reported without credentials."
  ],
